+// r35 S3 Rev 7 (Akiza review 537f3776, RULES-Q-17; Claude 28 Oct 2026). SELF-VERIFIED (builder = verifier), NOT independent.
+// NATIVE gate fixture for the Kashtira punish timing (Kashtira 19 Oct list vs a Blue-Eyes hand-trap holder).
+// Kashtira (seat 0, going first) controls face-up Kashtira Fenrir, Unicorn and Ogre and activates Fenrir's search.
+//  K1 (Ash): the punishes are NOT chain responses (not offered while Ash is on the chain); after the chain resolves Unicorn
+//      and Ogre are offered; Fenrir is not (we control no face-up card to target); a face-up Kashtira Birth never punishes
+//      a hand trap (Spells only); Ash still resolves (the search is negated).
+//  K2 (Imperm on Fenrir, Preparations face-up): a Trap never triggers Fenrir / Unicorn / Ogre; Preparations' Trap punish
+//      is offered after the chain (face-up Preparations + a face-up Kashtira). K2b: a face-down Preparations does not.
+//  K3 (Imperm on Unicorn, then Ash on Ogre's search): the Imperm-negated Unicorn's punish banishes nothing for the rest of
+//      the turn (control without Imperm: it banishes 1). Engine divergence recorded: the negated effect is still offered.
+import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
+import {engine,stopEngine,scenario,drive,seatOf,labels,hand,M,R} from '../tools/s3-harness.mjs';
+await engine();
+const F='Kashtira Fenrir',U='Kashtira Unicorn',O='Kashtira Ogre',PREP='Kashtira Preparations',BIRTH='Kashtira Birth',ASH='Ash Blossom & Joyous Spring',IMPERM='Infinite Impermanence';
